I was shot about 16 years ago and I  still feel the effects from that day in  every aspect of my life  [Music]  I was working as a camp counselor when I  was 16 years old at the North Valley  Jewish Community Center one day after  playing capture the flag I was walking  in with one of my favorite campers we  decided to walk to the front of the  building because that's where the rest  of my campers were who were all five and  six year old kids and as we walked to  the front of the building a man walked  in carrying a semi-automatic hoozy  replica gun and started shooting and he  shot off about 70 rounds of ammunition  into the building he shot me first and  then he just started spraying he showed  up on a day where there were a lot of  children there about 350 kids at the  Jewish Community Center so I grabbed  James and I ran into a classroom that  was right in front of us and there were  a bunch of little kids five and six  years old in that room with my co  counselors and I was covered in blood  and we still heard shooting outside  bang bang bang the campers all looked up  at me and kept saying what's all over  Mindy what's all over Mindy there  happened to be an emergency exit in that  one room that we went into we ran  outside there was a glass sliding door  behind us and he saw us running and shot  through the glass door and the glass  exploded behind us I had lost a lot of  blood at that point and couldn't  continue running so we closed our eyes  and played dead until we heard sirens  and to this day I still have quite a bit  of shrapnel inside my leg and it's a  constant reminder of what I went through  the thing that I remember most is when  you breathe in you feel air inside your  lungs but you've never felt air anywhere  else inside your body and immediately  after the bullets passed through me I  remember feeling invisible because there  was air running through me that I had  never felt before  and that's the instant that I knew  something a wasn't right  B I had been shot and the moment where I  started thinking about death he shot  three five-year-old kids myself who was  16 at the time and a 65 year old woman  who was the receptionist the ones that  weren't shot they are you know in their  20s now and are continuing to have  horrific nightmares about this bad man  with a gun coming in trying to take  their lives away a year later I tried to  go away to college and I had a complete  breakdown within the first six days of  being there a kid walked down the hall  with a nerf gun and he was just you know  having fun laughing and and shooting  everybody with nerf balls and the second  the Nerf ball hit me I broke down they  put me in a psych ward of a hospital and  I felt crazy so I typically have a panic  attack every time I see a mass shooting  Virginia Tech immediately after I had a  panic attack Sandy Hook instantly panic  attack and I know moving forward I will  continue to have the reactions like I do  what scares me is not having the  reaction it scares me  when we become numb people always tell  me that I was in the wrong place at the  wrong time but in reality I was in the  right place at the right time I was 16  you know I was working with my little  kids I was protecting my kids and our  future as a society and so how dare you  tell me I was in the wrong place at the  wrong time he was in the wrong place at  the wrong time  I think it happened to me for a reason I  don't think there are a lot of people  that could have handled what happened to  me as well as I have I've definitely  suffered emotionally I continue to  suffer I'm 33 I'm married I own a home I  live in a wonderful wonderful city and I  couldn't be happier and had I not been  shot all of those things probably  wouldn't necessarily have happened to me  but yeah I would take it away I don't  put this on anybody but if it could have  happened anybody I am glad it happened  to me because nobody deserves to go  through that kind of pain  [Music]
 

